Do not claim SMP when a secondary CPU was dropped.

0155 stopped panicking on a secondary bring-up timeout and dropped the CPU
instead, but the code right after the start loop still published SMP to the
rest of the kernel (ml_cpu_init_completed, cpusRunning, the
gIOAllCPUInitializedKey resource and ml_set_max_cpus(4)).  With only the boot
CPU actually online the machine layer then addresses CpuDataEntries for CPUs
that never came up, which faulted immediately - the panel showed a panic and
the boot never reached userspace, so the SWEETLOG flusher never ran and the
SMP diagnostics were lost again (the userdata ring still showed the previous
boot's "requested=1").

This patch keeps the machine a 1-CPU machine when any CPU was dropped: it logs
"N/M CPUs initialized, K dropped -> staying a 1-CPU machine" and returns
without touching the SMP publish calls, so the boot continues into userspace,
the flusher writes the console ring (mark/stage, GICC readback, sig_raw,
AFFINITY_INFO and the DROPPED line) to the userdata tail, and the next
unattended cycle reads it back from TWRP.
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetCPU.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetCPU.cpp
@@ -655,7 +655,24 @@
 		IOLog("SWEET CPU: cpu=%u mpidr=0x%x came alive; SGI1 OK\n",
 		    i, topology->cpus[i].phys_id);
 	}
-	/* Publish exactly once, after every selected CPU has completed initCPU(). */
+	/*
+	 * Publish exactly once, after every selected CPU has completed initCPU().
+	 *
+	 * 0156: if any CPU was dropped we must NOT claim SMP to the rest of the
+	 * kernel.  ml_set_max_cpus(4) with only one CPU online makes the machine
+	 * layer address CpuDataEntries for CPUs that never came up, which is what
+	 * turned 0155's graceful drop into a hard fault right afterwards.  Stay a
+	 * 1-CPU machine instead: the boot continues into userspace, the SWEETLOG
+	 * flusher writes the console ring - including all SMP diagnostics printed
+	 * above - to the userdata tail, and the next unattended cycle reads it.
+	 */
+	if (sweet_smp_dropped != 0) {
+		IOLog("SWEET CPU: %u/%u CPUs initialized, %u dropped -> staying "
+		    "a %u-CPU machine (SMP diagnostics above are in the log)\n",
+		    topology->num_cpus - sweet_smp_dropped, topology->num_cpus,
+		    sweet_smp_dropped, topology->num_cpus - sweet_smp_dropped);
+		thread_terminate(current_thread());
+	}
 	ONC_STAGE(0xB5);
 	ml_cpu_init_completed();
 	ONC_STAGE(0xB6);
